# Web app (Next.js 16)

- Read `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` when using App Router APIs — differs from Next 14 training data.
- Server Components by default; `"use client"` only when needed (hooks, events, browser APIs).
- Supabase: `createClient()` from `@/lib/supabase/server` in actions/RSC; `@/lib/supabase/client` in client components.
- Prefer existing UI in `components/ui/` before adding dependencies.
- Analytics: `trackEvent` from `@/lib/analytics` for user actions in rooms.

## Middleware (`src/middleware.ts`)

- **`config.matcher` must be a static literal array of strings** — Next.js/Turbopack cannot parse imported or spread matchers. Build fails on Amplify if violated.
- Keep matcher paths in sync with `isProtectedAppPath()` in `lib/auth/middleware-routes.ts` (comment both files when editing).
- Public routes (`/`, `/rooms`, `/leaderboard`) stay **out** of matcher to avoid blocking TTFB on `getUser()`.
- Skill: `.cursor/skills/studyverce-auth/SKILL.md`

## Navbar & TTFB

- `navbar.tsx` — static shell only (no async server `getUser()`).
- `navbar-interactive.tsx` — client auth hydration via `getNavbarAuthState()`.
- Do not reintroduce server-side profile/friend fetches in the root layout.

## Auth pages

- Use `components/auth/password-input.tsx` for password fields.
- Password reset success: `window.location.assign("/dashboard?password_reset=success")`; `QueryToastHandler` shows toast (not `router.push`).
- Skill: `.cursor/skills/studyverce-auth/SKILL.md`
